#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0328 expect=skipped domain=TE
#note "AUTHORED BY Plan B phase 4d. CDISC-CG0328 already carried BOTH single-column-absent arms (-invalid_tedur_absent-TE and -invalid_teenrl_absent-TE) and neither moved under the adoption -- one listed column is still present in each, so the Any leg is satisfied and the rule fires exactly as before. What it had NO scenario for was the all-absent case, which is the only case Requirements.Variables.Any [TEENRL, TEDUR] changes: NEITHER column is declared here, so the leg is unmet and the rule SKIPS instead of folding dataset-constant TRUE and emitting one finding at row 1. The all-absent case is nothing-to-check, not a defect (M2-D24 / M3-F.1). DIRECTION PIN: this file and the two -absent siblings must be read as a set. Were the Any leg wired as a conjunction (skip as soon as ANY entry is absent) both siblings would go SKIPPED and RED; were the leg dropped altogether this file would fire and go RED. Only the set fixes the direction. The Check here is byte-identical to CDISC-CG0329's, CORE-000027's, FDA-SD0089's and PMDA-SD0089's, so a regression in the Any leg surfaces on all five at once. Both findings snapshots are structurally blind (te.json and phuse's te.xpt each carry both columns) -- Gate C evidence."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent
CDISCPILOT01 | TE | TRT  | Treatment | First dose
